      "id": 200312,
      "name": "arenson9",
      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-07-20T04:01:19.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Bigbywolfe\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/dbc845/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Bigbywolfe:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This reorganization us terrible for me. Instead of checking one \"Active topic\" category that had every thing I was interested in (Sentinel Comics) I now have to check seven active topic categories.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Interesting. I've always used the 'New &amp; updated topics' tab, but I can certainly see why this would be worse for you.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I supposed what would be good is the ability to configure a set of topics of interest and then just always see those. I'll ping the forum maintainter to see if such a thing would be easy to implement, but don't hold your breath.</p>",
